        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add gated Claw hosted feed and lifecycle proof",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- publish a separate `/api/v1/feeds/claws` catalog feed only when `CLAWHUB_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`\n- include safe validated manifest summaries plus exact package version and digest, never the full Claw manifest\n- fail closed with 404 and `no-store` while disabled, including when a stale publication exists\n- prove the hosted lifecycle by resolving, downloading, digest-checking, safely extracting, and passing a fixture to real OpenClaw `claws add --dry-run --json`\n- route `/feeds/claws` permanently to the versioned feed, matching existing feed conventions\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: openclaw/rfcs#27\n- Depends on: #3091\n- This is ClawHub PR 4 of 4. It remains draft and experimental.\n\n## Contract\n\nClaws use a dedicated feed so existing plugin-feed consumers never encounter an unknown entry variant. Feed publication and serving share the exact experimental gate. Only official, visible, security-eligible Claw releases with a digest and stored validated manifest/summary are projected. ClawHub owns discovery and artifact integrity; OpenClaw owns preview, consent, and mutation. The experimental feed is intentionally not advertised through the static well-known registry document.\n\nThe cross-repository proof rejects absolute or parent-relative archive paths and all link or special-file entries before extraction. It then verifies the downloaded digest and invokes OpenClaw in an isolated state directory.\n\n## Validation\n\n- focused feed, API, schema, redirect, archive-safety, and E2E suites pass\n- real cross-repo proof against OpenClaw PR #106888 head `1b00790e260`: downloaded package produces a non-mutating `openclaw.clawAddPlan.v1` plan\n- malicious symlink archive regression passes\n- `bun run ci:static`\n- `bun run ci:types-build`\n- structured Codex review against the refreshed #3091 head: clean, no actionable findings\n\nThe structured review sandbox could not bind localhost (`EPERM`); the same hosted E2E passed outside that sandbox before and after the archive hardening.",
        "branch": "user/giodl/clawhub-claws-feed",
